   "project": "fieldnotes",
   "reply": "Yes, `list` follows the ISO-8601 rule.\n\n- **Storage:** `store.add` in `fieldnotes/store.py:24` saves `created` as `moment.isoformat()`. The moment is UTC-aware, so the value looks like `2026-01-02T03:04:05+00:00`.\n- **Printing:** `list` in `fieldnotes/cli.py` prints `note['created']` as it was stored. It doesn't reformat it, and it uses no `strftime` or locale formatting.\n- **Other output:** `add` prints only the note text, with no date. A grep for date and time handling found nothing else that prints a date.\n\nOne gap: nothing enforces this. If a note's `created` value were ever written in another format, `list` would print it unchanged. Today's only writer is `add`, so that can't happen yet.\n\nI can add a test that runs `list` and checks the printed date is ISO-8601, if you want a guard.",
