   "project": "fieldnotes",
   "reply": "I added `fieldnotes export`, which prints one `DATE: TEXT` line per note, and the project checks pass (2 tests OK, no lines over 100 characters).\n\n- **Command:** `export` is in `fieldnotes/cli.py`, backed by a small `export_lines()` helper. I also moved the usage string into one constant and added `export` to it.\n- **Date format:** DATE is the date part of the note's timestamp, for example `2026-01-02: first`. If you'd rather have the full ISO timestamp, it's a one-line change.\n- **Test:** `tests/test_cli.py` adds two notes, runs `cli.main([\"export\"])`, and checks the exit code and output.\n- **Checks:** `tools/check.py` needs `NOTES_HOME` set, and it wasn't set here. I pointed it at a throwaway temp directory instead of a real notes location, so your own notes weren't touched.",
